b)	Implement a Simple data access application using JDBC
Aim: To design and implement a transactional database application using the Spring JDBC module and JdbcTemplate to perform simple CRUD query executions on an in-memory database.

Procedure:
•	Initialize a Spring Boot project via Spring Initializr with JDBC API and H2 Database dependencies. 
•	Create an entity class named Product to represent stored data records.
•	Construct a repository class leveraging Spring's JdbcTemplate to execute structured raw SQL commands.
•	Establish a Command Line Runner component to initialize the database table and seed records upon startup.
•	Run the main class to verify operational log outputs in the terminal. 
